/***************************************************************
 * SCRIPT: CAT-1-SquareCatalogSync-v26.2.1
 * SYSTEM: ADC|IBC POS Backend
 * TABLE(S): PROCESSOR CATALOG MAP, ITEM LIBRARY, PROCESSOR CATEGORY MAP
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Batch creates/updates Square PRODUCTION catalog items and item
 * variations from PROCESSOR CATALOG MAP records.
 *
 * VERSIONING:
 * CAT-1-SquareCatalogSync-v26.2.1
 *
 * Version format:
 * - CAT-1 = item/catalog sync workflow/script number.
 * - v26 = 2026 system standard.
 * - .2 = major structural update: single-record item sync converted to
 *        batch item/variation sync.
 * - .1 = bug fixes
 *
 * SCRIPT BEHAVIOR:
 * 1. Runs when one PROCESSOR CATALOG MAP record enters the Ready for
 *    Catalog Sync view.
 * 2. Uses that trigger as a batch kick-off.
 * 3. Processes all eligible PROCESSOR CATALOG MAP records where:
 *    - Catalog Processor = SQUARE
 *    - Processor Environment = PRODUCTION
 *    - Sync to Processor? = checked
 *    - Sync Status = READY TO SYNC
 * 4. Groups catalog map records into Square parent ITEM objects by:
 *    - Processor Item Name
 *    - Processor Category
 * 5. Each PROCESSOR CATALOG MAP record becomes one Square ITEM_VARIATION.
 * 6. All sibling variations in the same group receive the same:
 *    - Processor Item ID
 * 7. Each variation receives its own:
 *    - Processor Variation ID
 *    - Processor Catalog Object ID
 * 8. Requires exactly one linked ITEM LIBRARY record per catalog-map record.
 * 9. Requires exactly one linked Processor Category record per catalog-map record.
 *    - If missing/multiple: sets Sync Status = NEEDS REVIEW.
 * 10. Requires linked Processor Category to already have a Processor Category ID.
 *    - If missing: sets Sync Status = SYNC ERROR.
 * 11. Assigns the linked specific category to Square using:
 *    - item_data.categories = [{ id: Processor Category ID }]
 *    - item_data.reporting_category = { id: Processor Category ID }
 * 12. Does NOT assign the parent category to Square.
 *    - Processor Parent Category remains Airtable-only reporting metadata.
 * 13. Uses Square Catalog Batch Upsert:
 *    - one request
 *    - multiple Square ITEM objects
 *    - each ITEM contains its grouped ITEM_VARIATION objects
 * 14. On success:
 *    - writes Processor Item ID
 *    - writes Processor Variation ID
 *    - writes Processor Catalog Object ID
 *    - writes Processor Catalog Version
 *    - sets Sync Status = SYNCED
 *    - sets Last Sync At = now
 *    - clears Sync Error
 *    - saves Raw Sync Response
 * 15. On failure:
 *    - sets READY TO SYNC records involved in the attempted batch to SYNC ERROR
 *    - writes Sync Error
 *    - saves Raw Sync Response if available
 *
 * UPDATES / BUG FIXES:
 * v26.2.1
 * - Minor text wrapping fix using trim() in input.config()
 *
 * v26.2.0
 * - Major structural change from single-record item sync to batch item sync.
 * - Groups sibling variation records into shared Square ITEM objects.
 * - Each PROCESSOR CATALOG MAP record now maps to a Square ITEM_VARIATION.
 * - All sibling variations now share the same Processor Item ID.
 * - Each variation keeps its own Processor Variation ID for inventory and sales tracking.
 * - Uses Processor Item Name + Processor Category as the grouping key.
 * - Assigns the linked Processor Category as both Square item category and reporting category.
 * - Uses Square Catalog Batch Upsert endpoint.
 *
 * v26.1.0
 * - Added support for updated PROCESSOR CATALOG MAP category mapping schema:
 *     Processor Category
 *     Processor Parent Category
 * - Required Processor Category to be linked before syncing.
 * - Used linked Processor Category ID as Square item category/reporting category.
 *
 * v26.0.1
 * - Fixed all-caps Airtable Sync Status option handling.
 *
 * v26.0.0
 * - Initial production Square item/catalog sync release.
 * - Created/updated one Square ITEM with one ITEM_VARIATION per triggering record.
 *
 * IMPORTANT:
 * - Processor Parent Category is not sent to Square.
 * - Processor Category must point to the specific category/subcategory that
 *   should be assigned to the Square item.
 * - CAT-0 must successfully sync Square categories before CAT-1 item sync.
 * - If one sibling variation is READY TO SYNC, this script may also include
 *   already-SYNCED sibling records in the same Square item group so that
 *   the Square item can be rebuilt with the full variation set.
 *
 * REQUIRED AIRTABLE AUTOMATION INPUTS:
 * - catalogMapRecordId
 *
 * REQUIRED AIRTABLE SECRET:
 * - SQUARE_PRODUCTION_ACCESS_TOKEN
 ***************************************************************/

